@startuml review-decision
title Presserl – Approval chain (author A, section S)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans-Serif

start
:A writes an article in S;
:chain = levels above A's highest role in S\n(section editor → editor-in-chief → publisher)\nwithout skipped levels;
note right
  A level is **skipped** when
  • no account other than A holds its role
    (locked accounts count), or
  • someone of that level trusts A (planned).
end note
if (chain empty?) then (yes)
  :A clicks **Publish**;
else (no)
  :A clicks **Submit**;
  repeat
    :waits for the lowest level left\n(never published: status **Submitted**;\npublished/offline: status and live revision stay;\ncontent frozen);
    :one person ≠ A holding this level's role\nor a higher one decides;
    if (decision) then (reject)
      :submission ends, note to A\n(never published → **Draft**);
      stop
    else (approve)
      :every level up to the\napprover's level is settled;
    endif
  repeat while (a staffed level above\nthe approver's level left?) is (yes)
endif
:**Published** (latest revision live);
stop

note left
  Solo: the first account holds all roles
  → empty chain → published at once.
  A may **withdraw** a submission at any time.
  Levels are re-evaluated at every approval.
end note
@enduml
